<title>CANADA: Canada's international travel account gap shrinks.</title>
<headline>Canada's international travel account gap shrinks.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Higher spending by foreign visitors and less Canadian tourist spending abroad cut the deficit in Canada's international travel account by 26.5 percent in the second quarter, Statistics Canada said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The deficit fell to a seasonally adjusted C$715 million in the second quarter from C$973 million in the first, as foreigners spent a record C$3.00 billion seasonally adjusted while Canadians reduced their spending abroad by 5.1 percent to C$3.72 billion.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Burea (613) 235-6745</p>
